{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Specialist Prompt Contracts.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Specialist Prompt Contracts.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"specialist prompt contracts specialist prompt contracts","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Specialist Prompt Contracts.md","fileName":"Specialist Prompt Contracts.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Specialist Prompt Contracts","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Multi-Agent Incident Response]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Multi-Agent Incident Response","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Specialist Prompt Contracts.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Specialist Prompt Contracts.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"specialist prompt contracts specialist prompt contracts","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Specialist Prompt Contracts.md","fileName":"Specialist Prompt Contracts.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Specialist Prompt Contracts","heading":"Specialist Prompt Contracts","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Specialist prompt contracts give each incident agent one responsibility and one structured result. A deployment analyst focuses on pipeline evidence, an application-health analyst focuses on runtime symptoms, and a runbook agent recommends only actions supported by the supplied runbook.\n\nEach contract treats operational text as untrusted, forbids destructive instructions, and requires JSON fields suited to the role. This prevents specialists from competing to solve the whole incident and makes their outputs easier to validate, compare, and combine during final synthesis.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Multi-Agent Incident Response","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF